{"causes": ["The societal and religious upheaval initiated by Muhammad's prophetic claims directly challenged the established polytheistic traditions and power structures of pre-Islamic Mecca.", "Umm Jamil's deep familial ties to the Quraish elite, particularly her marriage to Abu Lahab, aligned her with those who felt their authority and ancestral customs threatened by Islam.", "The economic and political rivalries among Meccan clans, including the Hashim and Abd Shams, fueled personal animosity towards Muhammad and his message."], "effects": ["Umm Jamil's prominent opposition contributed to the early persecution faced by the Muslim community in Mecca, intensifying the struggle for the nascent faith.", "Her actions and persona led to her direct condemnation in the Quran (Surah Al-Masad), cementing her role as an archetypal antagonist within Islamic scripture and theology.", "Her story served as a moral exemplar for early Muslims, reinforcing the concept of divine retribution against those who actively reject and harm prophets."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "muhammad", "sourceName": "Muhammad", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "umm-jamil", "targetName": "Umm Jamil", "context": "Muhammad's prophetic mission and message were the direct cause of Umm Jamil's intense opposition and animosity during the early 7th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "abu-lahab", "sourceName": "Abu Lahab", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "umm-jamil", "targetName": "Umm Jamil", "context": "Umm Jamil was married to Abu Lahab, and they collaboratively opposed the Islamic prophet Muhammad, leading to their joint condemnation in the Quran's Surah Al-Masad."}, {"sourceSlug": "umm-jamil", "sourceName": "Umm Jamil", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "surah-al-masad", "targetName": "Surah Al-Masad", "context": "Umm Jamil's actions and character directly influenced the content of Surah Al-Masad (Quran, Chapter 111), which explicitly condemns her and her husband, Abu Lahab."}, {"sourceSlug": 